</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2474-8-42-6"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Demographics of Validation Study Participants</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td align="left"><bold>Controls (n = 19)</bold></td><td align="left"><bold>Subjects (n = 17)</bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Age (yrs)</td><td align="left">32 (12)</td><td align="left">32 (12)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Sex</td><td align="left">11 females, 8 males</td><td align="left">9 females, 8 males</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Flexion (lbs of F)</td><td align="left">34.11 (14.67)</td><td align="left">30.46 (14.30)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Abduction (lbs of F)</td><td align="left">33.75 (14.20)</td><td align="left">30.55 (13.41)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">DASH</td><td align="left">1.10 (1.57)</td><td align="left">10.25 (12.57)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">SPADI</td><td align="left">1.26 (2.40)</td><td align="left">16.41 (18.60)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Test 1 (secs)</td><td align="left">300 (0)</td><td align="left">300 (0)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Test 2 (secs)</td><td align="left">290 (25)</td><td align="left">246 (74)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Test 3 (secs)</td><td align="left">300 (0)</td><td align="left">275 (51)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Ave. total time (secs)</td><td align="left">297 (8)</td><td align="left">274 (34)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>Mean (Standard Deviation)</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Pearson correlations between the FIT-HaNSA tasks and strength or self-report scores</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td align="center"><bold>Task 1</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Task 2</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Task 3</bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left"><bold>Flexion strength</bold></td><td align="center">--</td><td align="center">0.29<break/>(n = 36)</td><td align="center">0.15<break/>(n = 36)</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>Abduction strength</bold></td><td align="center">--</td><td align="center">0.27<break/>(n = 36)</td><td align="center">0.12<break/>(n = 36)</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>DASH</bold></td><td align="center">-0.83**<break/>(n = 41)</td><td align="center">-0.82**<break/>(n = 41)</td><td align="center">-0.73**<break/>(n = 41)</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>SPADI</bold></td><td align="center">-0.74**<break/>(n = 41)</td><td align="center">-0.76**<break/>(n = 41)</td><td align="center">-0.67**<break/>(n = 41)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>** Correlation is significant at the 0.01 level (2-tailed).</p><p>Note: The correlations between task 1 and strength could not be computed because all subjects completed the 300-seconds task.</p><p>The correlations between the tasks and self-report scores included the 5 patients from the development phase (part 1).</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>